<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE cygnus-ng25-2026-11-29 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 Cygnus NG-25 (SLC-40) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 8.80 s, kick 1.819 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 10500 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.1867-0.000127*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
ILLUSTRATIVE. PRE-FLIGHT. Cygnus XL NG-25 (S.S. Jim Lovell), Falcon 9, SLC-40, to the ISS. T0 2026-11-29T15:47:00Z. LL2 id d74afbc7-0de5-491c-be05-4e9c31f736ac Go, NET 15:47Z, window fields both 15:47Z, last_updated 2026-11-26T11:44:54Z. SpaceX https://www.spacex.com/launches/ng25 prose targets 10:47 a.m. ET. SOURCE CONFLICT: the page header is the window 10:40-11:00 ET (15:40-16:00Z). Used 15:47Z. Backup 30 Nov 10:24 a.m. ET = 2026-11-30T15:24:00Z. Ninth flight. Landing LZ-40.
Published timeline (SpaceX ng25): Max-Q 1:08, MECO 2:13, stage sep 2:17, flip 2:21, SES-1 2:24, boostback 2:30-3:21, fairing 2:53, entry 6:09-6:26, landing burn 7:24, LZ-40 landing 7:49, SECO-1 8:32, Cygnus XL deploys 14:35.
Target 245 x 245 km is the NG factsheet initial orbit, inclination printed there 51.64 deg. Azimuth 46.36 deg is from NAVAREA IV 1141/26 Area B and is not retuned. Deploy T+875 s is the SpaceX &#x27;Cygnus XL Deploys&#x27; mark. Booster recovery is not modelled.
Target (see launch config): insertion 245 km, apoapsis 245 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 46.36 deg; payload 10500 kg.
Pad: 28.561941N -80.577357E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-29T15:47:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: after final cutoff T+512.0 s the stage coasts (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model) to PAYLOAD DEPLOY T+875 s; rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF deploy T+875 s (https://www.spacex.com/launches/ng25 Cygnus XL Deploys T+00:14:35): alt 249.54 km, osculating 237.3 x 245.2 km, i 47.162 deg.</description>
